82 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 66 0 R
/E (Anglers Riverfly Monitoring Initiative \(ARMI\) score is an indicator of the river's ecological health. It is calculated by adding the 'sensitivity scores' of Urban Riverfly species sampled. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
83 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 66 0 R
/E (For this, higher values are assigned to pollution-sensitive species, and this score increases when they are recorded in higher numbers. The opposite is used for more pollution tolerant species. Higher ARMI scores suggest healthier ecosystems and better water quality \(i.e., less polluted\) conditions.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
84 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 66 0 R
/E (But there are things to bear in mind \(these things are never straight forward\)! ARMI can depend on how effectively species are being recorded - such as a size 10 welly collecting more bugs than a size 5 one! Also, the ARMI score has not been widely tested to Urban Riverfly, so Birmingham River Champion's \(BRC\) data will help improve the reliability of this national recording scheme \(see here for further details\).)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [8 183 0 R 10]
>>
endobj
