<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 71 0 R
/E (Across the Cole sites and their tributaries, ARMI scores were often higher during spring \(March-April\) and autumn \(September-October\). This likely reflects the life cycles of mayflies and caddisflies, where many species mature up to late spring/early summer, then emerge as winged adults before laying eggs that form into new generations that start becoming abundant again in autumn.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
123 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 71 0 R
/E (Lower scores were more common during summer \(light grey\) and winter \(dark grey\), which was clear for the Chinn Brook site in particular. This could be down to life cycles, but also could be when pollution is intensified by low river flows \(/dilution\) or high runoff washing contaminants into the channel during wet weather. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
