/T (As found for the Cole, higher ARMI scores were generally recorded during spring and autumn. This again likely reflects the life cycles of aquatic insects, which are particularly abundant here, whereby the number of their larvae increase in the build up to and after they have emerged as winged adults in summer. )
/E (As found for the Cole, higher ARMI scores were generally recorded during spring and autumn. This again likely reflects the life cycles of aquatic insects, which are particularly abundant here, whereby the number of their larvae increase in the build up to and after they have emerged as winged adults in summer. )
