558 0 obj
<<
/Title (Recently, ARMI scores along the Cole at Blackberry Way and Green Road weir dropped to the trigger level threshold, so we shall return soon to see whether scores go back up - the Environment Agency can investigate if trigger levels are breached twice consecutively)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 530 0 R
/Next 561 0 R
>>
endobj
559 0 obj
<<
/Title (The Rea at Cannon Hill park displayed considerable variability, with ARMI scores ranging between 2-14. Particularly low values were recorded in late winter to spring this year, but seem to have picked up slightly as the year has gone on. Encouragingly, strong increases in ARMI scores were observed at the Stone Brook in Ley Hill Park recently, and to a lesser extent both sites along the Bartley Brook in Senneleys Park.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 562 0 R
/Next 531 0 R
>>
endobj
560 0 obj
<<
/Title <>
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 481 0 R
/Prev 532 0 R
/Next 533 0 R
>>
endobj
561 0 obj
<<
/Title (However, as discussed in a recent report of ours, ARMI may not always fully reflect the presence of particularly sensitive species. For example, the pollution-sensitive stone clinger \(flat-bodied mayfly\) has been recorded at Scribers Lane and The Dingles, but has not been found further downstream at Green Road or Blackberry Way.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 558 0 R
/Next 563 0 R
>>
endobj
562 0 obj
<<
/Title <>
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 564 0 R
/Next 559 0 R
>>
endobj
563 0 obj
<<
/Title (Time series plots showing how ARMI scores change over time across Birmingham River Champions sites along the upper Cole)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 561 0 R
/Next 565 0 R
>>
endobj
564 0 obj
<<
/Title (However, opposite to what we found in the Cole, the Rea in Cannon Hill Park appears to be display lower ARMI scores during spring and autumn months, notably dropping below its trigger level in April this year \(but only once\).)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 566 0 R
/Next 562 0 R
>>
endobj
565 0 obj
<<
/Title (Time series plots showing how ARMI scores change over time across Birmingham River Champions sites along the upper Cole tributaries)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 563 0 R
/Next 567 0 R
>>
endobj
566 0 obj
<<
/Title (Comparing ARMI time series along the main Rea is more challenging than the Cole due to differences in sampling dates, and also these sites are more spread out.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 567 0 R
/Next 564 0 R
>>
endobj
